& [JustificationIdentity] is the bounded ingestion rationale
  + [justification_uuid] is a1687296-09d0-460a-aeff-0f4a660a2572
  + [conversation_uuid] is cab190f5-eda0-44e0-81a5-51f9605e0baa
  + [reserved_solution_uuid] is bb88172a-e70e-4a1a-aba3-20dfa572ec40

& [Claim] is deterministic SOP ingestion is the strongest next product increment
  + [support] is Cantor already signs, admits, indexes, queries, proves, transports, and caches programmatic SemanticUnit fixtures
  + [support] is the remaining gap between prototype and self-hosting product is governed source parsing and artifact construction
  + [support] is the user's intended semantic fabric requires exact lines, signatures, relationships, and queryable proof
  + [support] is a bounded parser can be tested exhaustively while unrestricted semantic interpretation cannot
  + [confidence] is high for the bounded profile and provisional for future full SOP coverage
  + [counterargument] is a partial grammar may appear to reduce SOP's intended expressiveness
  + [answer] is name the profile honestly, reject unsupported forms, preserve exact bytes, and add semantics only through later signed profiles
  + [invalidation_condition] is silent source loss, unstable identity, fabricated relation semantics, unverifiable quote, secret leakage, or inability to query real canonical files

& [SelectedApproach] is parse then lower then sign then verify then publish
  + [why] is parsing distinguishes syntax from semantic lowering
  + [why] is deterministic lowering gives PackageCompiler explicit inputs rather than model guesses
  + [why] is in-memory verification prevents publication of an unusable environment
  + [why] is existing protocol and adapters remain the execution oracle
  + [why] is a portable manifest makes the corpus reviewable and reproducible

& [Alternative] is train a neural ingestion model first
  + [status] is rejected_for_first_product_loop
  + [reason] is weights would obscure source-preserving semantics and add unexplained error before deterministic ground truth exists

& [Alternative] is import every SOP line as undifferentiated text
  + [status] is rejected
  + [reason] is it discards marker, scope, kind, containment, and fault meaning

& [Alternative] is implement the complete imagined SOP language now
  + [status] is deferred
  + [reason] is many operators lack settled executable semantics and guessing would violate specification governance

& [Alternative] is identify records by file and line
  + [status] is rejected
  + [reason] is relocation and insertion would destroy stable identity while anchors can retain human-readable file and line locations

& [DecisionClassification] is reversible and trust-sensitive
  + [decision_type] is type2_reversible
  + [rollback] is existing programmatic PackageCompilationInput and direct protocol execution remain available
  + [premortem] is permissive parsing, duplicate identity repair, path escape, key exposure, partial artifact publication, or success-only integration tests could create apparently signed but unfaithful fabric
  + [mitigation] is strict grammar, collision faults, canonical path containment, secret-free receipts, preflight verification, replacement control, and end-to-end exact-response tests

& [QualityBar] is SHI-AC1 through SHI-AC15
  = must: implement only the signed bounded profile
  = must: disclose unsupported forms and performance limits
  = must: record implementation contradictions as SJS rework
  - never: weaken the acceptance gate to preserve schedule
